  message: "Done in PR #3476. Runtime corpus-based coherence checker (the second half of ADR-0023 §3 enforcement, complementing the static drift linter) shipped as scripts/check-edge-type-runtime-coherence + hypergumbo_core.runtime_coherence + docs/edge-type-runtime-allowlist.yaml. Initial offender count on hypergumbo's own behavior map: 14 partitions across 91,898 edges; mostly legitimate construct distinctions (calls vs instantiates, contains vs extends) that will be allow-listed via ADR amendments as Phase 2/3 land. Implementation note documented in module docstring + ADR-0023 enforcement section: the partition key is four fields (src.kind, src.language, dst.kind, dst.language) rather than the six the ADR specifies, because hypergumbo doesn't store framework as a top-level Symbol field today; coarser key still catches every leak the finer key would. Deployment posture: warn-only (CLI returns exit 1 on un-allow-listed offenders for human invocation during Phase 2/3 migration; not yet wired into pre-commit / CI per the Phase-1 framing in ADR-0023 §6)."  # e7d1
